<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">separation</ansi>

Your company goes where you go. Walking through an exit, your companions
follow on foot. Any other way you are moved takes them too: a secret
passage, a trapdoor, a rope down a chasm, a portal, an inn room, a
journey's arrival, a quest that sends you somewhere, waking at a church
after you die, or the training grounds.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Who comes with you</ansi>

  Every living companion standing in the room you leave goes with you,
  and you see "Your company comes with you." A companion fighting beside
  you is taken out of that fight with you.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Not while you're fighting</ansi>

  A move you ask for yourself (pressing a hidden catch, climbing down a
  rope, springing a trap) waits until the battle is over:
  "Not while your company is fighting." A move done to you (dying,
  being dragged off to a cell, a trap someone else springs) still
  happens, and takes your company with you.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Separated companions</ansi>

  A living companion who isn't with you when you are moved is separated,
  and you're told who and why:

    Bryn was not with you and is separated from the company.

  A companion left behind for two rounds for any other reason (a door it
  couldn't pass, say) is separated the same way.

  A separated companion is off the map. Nothing can hurt or rob it, and
  it keeps its health, mana, wounds, gear, level, and place in your
  formation exactly as they were. While it's away it doesn't recover,
  eat, tire, earn experience, or carry anything for the company, and its
  pack doesn't count toward your cargo room.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Finding the way back</ansi>

  A separated companion rejoins you wherever you are after about a
  minute (15 rounds, as the world ships). The minute only counts while
  you're logged in: logging out pauses it, and logging back in doesn't
  bring anyone back early. If the time is up while you're in a battle,
  on a journey, or resting at camp, it waits and rejoins when that's
  over. It never walks into a fight.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">The fallen, the fled, and your herd</ansi>

  A move never touches a fallen companion: it stays on your roster,
  waiting to be raised at any church or village shaman within its time
  (<ansi fg="command">help resurrect</ansi>), and wakes beside you when raised.
  A companion who fled a battle rejoins you wherever you are once the
  battle is settled (<ansi fg="command">help morale</ansi>).
  Your horses and your company's cargo always go with you
  (<ansi fg="command">help mount</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help cargo</ansi>).

<ansi fg="command">company status</ansi> shows a separated companion and how long until it's
back; the web client's Company and Vitals panels mark it as separated.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help company</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help travel</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help death</ansi>,
<ansi fg="command">help readiness</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help retreat</ansi>.
